# The composition line: the name of the song, the AMPLE version it is written for (ample 1), the tempo in beats per minute and the master seed.
# tip: change the tempo (120) to hear it faster or slower; the notes keep their place in the bars.
composition "A sine tone" { ample 1  tempo 120  master-seed 20261017 }

# midi-clip "tune": A clip of notes: it makes no sound itself, it feeds the notes to an instrument.
# tip: in a melody, a note is name:length (c4:1 is middle C for one beat); r:1 is a rest.
midi-clip tune at 1 for 2 {
  melody "a4:8"
  bars 2
}

# synth "voice": An instrument: it turns the notes it gets into sound with an oscillator.
#   wave is the shape of the tone, attack and release shape its start and end, cutoff takes away high frequencies.
# tip: try "wave saw" for a brighter, buzzier tone, or "wave sine" for a soft, round one.
# tip: gain is the level in dB; -6 dB is about half as loud.
synth voice at 1 for 2 {
  wave sine
  sustain 100
  gain -12 dB
  from tune.notes -> notes
}

# master "out": The master: what reaches it is what you hear. Every song has exactly one.
master out {
  from voice.audio -> audio
}

# The composition line: the name of the song, the AMPLE version it is written for (ample 1), the tempo in beats per minute and the master seed.
# tip: change the tempo (120) to hear it faster or slower; the notes keep their place in the bars.
